The diagram is an enlarged view of one microsporangium of a young anther, seen in transverse section as a nearly circular structure. Its wall has four layers, labelled from outside in:
- **Epidermis**, the outermost layer;
- **Endothecium**;
- **Middle layers**;
- **Tapetum**, the innermost layer.

The centre of the microsporangium is occupied by the **sporogenous tissue**, a group of compactly arranged homogenous cells.

Functions:
- **Outermost layer (epidermis)**: with the endothecium and middle layers, it performs the function of **protection** and helps in **dehiscence of the anther** to release the pollen.
- **Innermost layer (tapetum)**: it **nourishes the developing pollen grains**. Its cells have dense cytoplasm and generally more than one nucleus.
